      "description": "Watch Estudiantes L.P. vs Defensa Y Justicia highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 1, 2026. Expectation hung heavy in the air as Estudiantes de La Plata hosted Defensa y Justicia in a high-stakes Liga Profesional Argentina encounter. Both sides took to the pitch on August 1, 2026 , looking to assert their dominance and secure a vital result in the league standings. Clinical First-Half Blitz The hosts wasted no time in stamping their authority on the match. In the 10th minute, Guido Carrillo opened the scoring after being played in by Eric Meza . The momentum stayed firmly with the home side, and by the 17th minute, the lead was doubled. Ezequiel Piovi found the back of the net following a sharp assist from Tiago Palacios , leaving the visitors reeling from the early pressure. As the first half progressed, the intensity shifted into a more physical battle. Yellow cards were shown to David Barbona , Fabricio Perez , and Damian Fernandez as frustrations began to mount for the away side. However, Estudiantes remained focused on their offensive duties. In the 36th minute, Tomas Palacios added a third goal, assisted by the influential Guido Carrillo , effectively deciding the contest before the halftime whistle. Tactical Shifts and Penalty Drama The second period saw a flurry of tactical changes, with Lucas Alario and Ramiro Funes Mori among those introduced to see out the game. While the scoring pace slowed, there was a late twist when Defensa y Justicia were awarded a penalty in the 87th minute. David Barbona stepped up with a chance to redeem his earlier booking, but his effort missed the target. The match ended shortly after, confirming a comprehensive and disciplined performance from Estudiantes ."
